{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And how will Pharaoh hear me.</b> This is one of ten a fortiori arguments in the Torah (Bereshit Rabbah 92)." "<b>Of uncircumcised lips.</b> Unclosed of lips; and so every term of עֲרָלָה I say is 'closed': ״עֲרֵלָה אָזְנָם״ (Jeremiah 6) — closed from hearing; ״עַרְלֵי לֵב״ (ibid. 9) — closed from understanding; ״שְׁתֵה גַּם אַתָּה וְהֵעָרֵל״ (Habakkuk 2) — and be closed from the drunkenness of the cup of the curse; עָרְלַת בָּשָׂר — the foreskin closed and covered by it; ״וַעֲרַלְתֶּם עָרְלָתוֹ״ (Leviticus 19) — make for it a closure and covering of obstruction that separates it from its eating; ״שָׁלֹשׁ שָׁנִים יִהְיֶה לָכֶם עֲרֵלִים״ (ibid.) — closed and covered and separated from eating it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:48.303509232Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}